# Astro AI Agent — Standards & Specs Map

Before writing or changing code, follow the coding standards under `docs/standards/`.
Start at [docs/standards/README.md](../../docs/standards/README.md) for the index of
what applies (coding, comments, testing, config, and related docs).

Before building or changing a feature, read the matching feature spec at
`docs/specs/<feature>.md`. Discover available specs via
[docs/specs/README.md](../../docs/specs/README.md).

## Workflow

1. **Standards first** — open `docs/standards/README.md`, then the specific
   standard docs that apply to the files you will touch.
2. **Specs before features** — open `docs/specs/README.md`, then
   `docs/specs/<feature>.md` for the feature under work.
3. **Brainstorming** — when using brainstorming "explore project context",
   include reading `docs/specs/README.md` (and relevant feature specs) so
   design work is grounded in existing product intent.

This rule is a **map only**. Do not treat this file as the source of standards
or specs; the authoritative content lives under `docs/standards/` and
`docs/specs/`.
